lock area). Center has two Goombas and a pipe. Right has a brick staircase going up. This is VERY similar to the start of 1-1 (the ? block + brick row + pipe + staircase). \n\nHmm, but the start of 1-1: ? block at x=256 (tile 32), then bricks at x≈352-384, then pipes at 448, 512... no staircase.\n\nActually is there a brick staircase at the start? No. The staircase near the end.\n\nI think the level has a \"second half\" that mirrors the first somewhat.\n\nHmm, hold on, let me reconsider the possibility that the previous session's save was at the START and my address math is wrong because 0x006D/0x0086 might have been read while the game was in a different state.\n\nNo — I verified with get_tile_at_pixel scroll_x=178, which is authoritative.\n\nWait, unless get_tile_at_pixel's scroll is in PPU tile units... no, 178 pixels.\n\nOK so camera low = 178 initially. If camera page was 0 (not 8), then camera = 178 and Mario absolute = 0x0086 + 0x006D*256 = 40 + 9*256 = 2344. Then Mario screen x = 2344-178 = 2166?? No, that's impossible.\n\nSo camera page must be 8. Hmm but I read 0x071A = 1818 which I didn't read initially. In the second watch, 0x071A was 9 while camera low 0x071C... wait in the first watch I watched 1820 (=0x71C) and got 179→120. In the second watch I watched 1818 (=0x71A) and got 9→10. OK.\n\nInitially: Mario page 0x6D = 9, low 40 → 2344. Camera low 0x71C = 178, page 0x71A presumably 8 → 2226. Screen x = 118. ✓.\n\nSo Mario was at 2344. And the scene at 2226-2482 was hill+bush (screenshot). In 1-1, what's at x 2226-2482? Given that the screenshot showed hill+bush+brick ground and a stepped brick structure... \n\nHmm, and now at 2837 we see ? block/Goombas/pipe/staircase. \n\nIn actual SMB 1-1: the famous \"three bricks with a hidden 1-up\" section? Let me recall: 1-1 has, near the end:\n- x≈2000: staircase of 4 blocks (the \"pyramid\")? \n- Then a pipe\n- Then the long staircase up to the flagpole.\n\nHmm.\n\nOK forget it; the empirical playback is what m