 $3D. Interesting. Actually in SMB the flagpole ball is tile $3D? Hmm, CHR $13D. Let me read_tile 0x13D to confirm it's a ball.\n\nWait — but there's a subtlety: the nametable is being written live; screen_box x=146 means the tile covers x146-153. The pole ball graphic centered.\n\nLet me now call get_region object mode at (150,95) for the flag and (151,130) for the pole.\n\nActually get_region object mode returns connected opaque pixels of same layer+palette. The pole and flag share palette 0 presumably. Let me test.\n\nLet me also call list_sprites to see if the flag is a sprite.\n\nLet me batch several calls."}
