r. If it's the sprite's left edge, then Mario occupies 898-914, and the pipe starts at 914 (screen 146). Then the screenshot's pipe at 120 doesn't match... \n\nUgh. Coordinates are confusing.\n\nLet me just use get_tile_at_pixel to locate the pipe precisely.\n\nBut more importantly: Mario is now FALLING. So we need to load state 3 (saved at x=898) and figure out the obstacle.\n\nHmm, but wait: if Mario fell at x=893 after retreating, then... maybe the \"pipe\" is actually a gap and the pipe graphic is beyond? Confusing.\n\nLet me load state 3 (x=898, standing, blocked) and inspect the tiles around.\n\nActually, since state 3 has Mario at x=898 grounded and blocked, let me load it and examine with get_tile_at_pixel at several points to map the region.\n\nLet me do that.\n\nActually, hold on. Maybe the whole issue is that the \"pipe\" is a 4-tile pipe that Mario can't jump over, and there's a pit right before it. Hmm — in SMB 1-1, there IS a section like that? No.\n\nHmm, wait. Let me reconsider the level. What if this is NOT the standard 1-1 layout but the ROM's 1-1 is different? The mapping said 1-1 layout records are at prgRom 0x2690, 49 records. A standard SMB 1-1 has ~? Actually the standard 1-1 layout data is 49 records — plausible.\n\nHmm, but the presence of a pit at x~893 with a tall pipe... \n\nOH WAIT. I think I might be misinterpreting. Let me reconsider: In SMB 1-1, there IS a pit! The level has a gap right before the pipe that goes to the coin room? No...\n\nHmm, actually yes! In SMB 1-1, after the two pipes at the start, there's a GAP in the ground (a pit) around x=1140? Hmm.\n\nHmm, actually I recall now: 1-1 has a pit right after the first set of pipes? Let me think about the level in terms of tiles... \n\nHonestly, let me just inspect. Load state 3.\n\nActually, maybe better: load state 3 and take a screenshot. Then use get_tile_at_pixel to map the ground.\n\nLet me do it."}
