r? Hmm.\n\nActually, yes! SMB 1-1 has progressively taller pipes near the start: pipes of height 2, 3, 4, 4? Hmm, maybe.\n\nHmm, in 1-1, the first pipe section: pipe at x=448 (2 high), x=512 (2 high), x=640 (3 high?), x=896 (4 high). Hmm.\n\nHmm, actually now I do recall 1-1 has a set of pipes where the last is 4 blocks tall and you must jump onto it and over. Mario CAN jump onto a 4-block pipe if he jumps from the ground with a running start? Actually, in SMB, Mario's jump height is 4 blocks when running at full speed, and 5 blocks with a \"running jump\" from... hmm.\n\nHmm, the practical way in 1-1: you approach the tall pipe with running speed and jump; Mario can reach the top if he has speed. Our problem: Mario was blocked against the pipe and lost all speed, so he couldn't jump onto it.\n\nSo the fix: back up far enough to build speed, then run and jump.\n\nOur earlier \"retreat 35 frames left\" only moved 5px — because Mario was blocked on the LEFT too?! Hmm, that suggests something on his left. Hmm, or because the \"left\" input doesn't work? Actually holding Left should move him left freely at 1.5px/frame → 52px. He moved 5px. So he was blocked on the left too.\n\nWhat's on his left? From the screenshot, at screen x~50-100 there were Goombas — not walls. Hmm.\n\nHmm, wait: maybe the y was changing during the \"left\" segment (he was in the air after a jump). At the start of that run, y=176 (ground), then y stayed 176 for ~26 frames (the left segment), then jumped. So during the left segment he was on the ground and should have moved left ~39px. He moved 5px.\n\nUnless the left input was blocked by... hmm.\n\nHmm, maybe x=125 is a wall: maybe Mario is at the RIGHT edge of a pit and moving left falls in? No, he'd fall.\n\nHmm, OR: Mario is stuck between the pipe (right) and a Goomba (left). The two Goombas were at screen ~50-100, so not adjacent.\n\nHmm, confusing. Let me just look at the current screenshot again and think.\n\nCurrent screenshot (state 3): \n