\n\nAnd ($071A,$071C) = camera left edge = 870.\n\nSo when I wrote $071A/$071C, the engine recomputed $071B/$071D from it (since $071D became 169, 233, etc.). Let me check: after writing $071C=41 (page 5), what did $071D become? I didn't read. Let me read $071A-$071F now.\n\nIf $071D is updated to camera+256 = 1321+256 = 1577 → page 6, low 41. So $071B=6, $071D=41.\n\nLet me verify.\n\nThen the spawner would spawn enemies at x ≤ 1577+0x30. The Koopas at 1456 are within. So they should spawn... unless the spawner index isn't there.\n\nHmm. Let me check the spawner index $0739 and page $073A. Read $0739 and $073A.\n\nLet me read $071A-$071F and $0739/$073A.\n\nActually, maybe the issue: the spawner only advances the index when it SPAWNS an enemy; if a slot is unavailable it waits. And if an enemy entry's x is far ahead, it waits. Since I jumped the camera, the entries behind the camera would be spawned and immediately despawn. Hmm.\n\nLet me just read the spawner index to see where it is.\n\n$0739 = 1849. $073A = 1850.\n\nLet me read."}
