erent area than the camera says. Hmm.\n\nHmm, but the screenshot shows Mario at screen x~0 with the level; if the camera were 1321 and Mario 1321, screen x 0 ✓.\n\nAnd the PPU scroll would be 1321 mod 256 = 41... but get_tile_at_pixel says 169. Hmm.\n\nHmm, unless get_tile_at_pixel's scroll_source \"scanline\" reads the actual PPU register which for the playfield is written per-scanline. Hmm.\n\nI'm going in circles with the camera internals. Let me focus on the OUTCOME: Is the level loading correctly and are the Koopas spawning?\n\nThe enemies aren't spawning. The spawner index $0739 = 11 (from read at 1849: [11,5,1,12] → $0739=11, $073A=5, $073B=1, $073C=12). So the spawner index is 11 and page $073A=5!\n\nIndex 11 corresponds to entry i=11: (03, 06) → x=0, y=48, type 6 (Goomba). Hmm, but wait, the spawner index counts bytes from the start of the list: index 11 = byte offset 11 = entry i=11. Yes.\n\nSo the spawner is at entry (03,06): page 5, x=0 → 1280, y=48, type 6. And $073A (page) = 5 → 1280. Hmm, and the camera is 1321, so the enemy at 1280 is behind the camera → it should spawn and despawn, advancing the index.\n\nHmm, but it's stuck at index 11. Hmm. Maybe because the enemy at x=1280 with y=48 spawns, but the slot is unavailable? Hmm.\n\nHmm, or maybe the spawner is stuck because the enemy at x=1280 is behind the camera and the code at $C1CB compares and branches to $C216 which... let me re-read $C216: `lda $06cb / bne / lda $0398 / cmp #1 / bne / lda #$2f / sta $16,x`. Hmm, that's the \"not spawned\" path? Confusing.\n\nHmm. Actually, maybe the spawner is waiting for a free slot and all slots show \"active\"? $000F-$0014 = 0, so slots are free.\n\nHmm, hmm.\n\nOK, let me step even more frames (e.g. 200) and see if the spawner advances. Maybe it needs the camera to be positioned just right.\n\nActually, hmm: the entry at index 11 has y=48 (high). The spawn code might reject enemies whose y is 0xE0? No.\n\nHmm, let me just step 120 frames and check.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: the spawner's page variable $073A=5 and the index=11 (entry i=11: x=0,y=48,type 6). If the spawner spawns it at page 5 + x 0 = 1280, y=48. That's on screen (camera 1321? then screen x = -41, off-screen left). Hmm, behind the camera → despawn immediately → index advances.\n\nUnless the spawner requires the enemy to be AHEAD of the camera to spawn, and skips behind-camera enemies WITHOUT advancing? Then it'd be stuck forever. Hmm.\n\nHmm, actually the code at $C1CF: `lda $06 / sbc $6e,x / bcc $C216` — if (screen_right - enemy_x) borrows (enemy ahead of screen right), go to $C216 (don't spawn). Otherwise fall through to spawn. So enemies behind the camera DO spawn (then despawn). So the index should advance.\n\nHmm, but $C216 sets $16,x = 0x2f (Toad?) if $06cb and $0398==1. Hmm, that's the \"not yet reached\" path.\n\nHmm, wait, I think I misread the branch. `bcc` = branch if carry clear = if borrow (screen_right < enemy_x). So if the enemy is beyond the screen right → branch to $C216 (wait). Otherwise → spawn. OK.\n\nSo at index 11, enemy x=1280, screen right = ~1577 → 1577 > 1280 → no borrow → spawn. So it should spawn.\n\nUnless the computed x uses the page incorrectly. $C1AB stores $073a into $6e,x (page) and byte0&0xF0 into $87,x (x low). For entry (03,06): byte0=0x03 → x low = 0x00; page=5 → x=1280. Screen right compare: ($071b,$071d) + 0x30 vs ($6e,$87). Hmm.\n\nOK whatever. Let me just step 200 frames and see.\n\nActually — maybe the problem is that the spawner only runs when the camera ACTUALLY moves (it's part of the scroll/level parser). If I write the camera and the engine doesn't consider it \"moved\" (because Mario isn't moving), the spawner may not run. Hmm.\n\nLet me instead WALK Mario right for a while — that moves the camera naturally and runs the parser. Mario at screen 0; walking right will scroll the camera.\n\nLet me hold right for 120 frames and see if enemies spawn.\n\nBut Mario is at level ~1321 (page 5?) and the Koopas 